{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Baseline maintenance: this story removes censused mechanism(s) — the legacy env-alias map `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES`/`_map_legacy_env` (`_config_sources.py:333-339`), the config-key alias table `_ALIASES` (`_config_sections.py:198`), and the 13 warn-class tombstone rows (`REBAR_PUSH`, `REBAR_RECONCILER_LOCK_MAX_RETRIES`, `REBAR_RECONCILER_LOCK_RETRY_BUDGET`, `REBAR_CODE_HEALTH_ANALYZERS`, `REBAR_CODE_HEALTH_ENABLED`, `REBAR_JIRA_RESOLVED_STATUSES`, `REBAR_RECONCILER_RESOLVED_STATUSES`; `reconciler.lock_backend`, `reconciler.lock_max_retries`, `code_health.analyzers`, `code_health.enabled`, `jira.resolved_statuses`, `reconciler.resolved_statuses`). Because `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py:357-364` asserts the committed baseline equals the live tree, run `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` in the same change and commit `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` (operator-sanctioned on the epic; precedent commit 81da792). State the sanction in the commit message.\n\nBaseline fact for the implementer (verified by grep of `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` on origin/main 083620b0): none of the names above has an `env_var::` / `config_key::` row (the tombstone registry stores them as data, not as `os.environ` reads, and both alias tables are empty), so `--update-stale` is expected to report nothing stale for this story; run it anyway per the epic sanction and commit the baseline only when it changes. `--check` must report `new=0` either way."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788807701677275536,"uuid":"3a7e2776-6abd-4488-845d-f887307be4db"}